    "timestamp": "2026-09-02T17:10:39.242000+00:00",
    "editedAt": "2026-09-02T17:11:10.910000+00:00",
    "content": "@everyone\n# **CoreFX 1.3.1 — Release Dates & New Monetization Policy**\n\n**Release schedule**\n• **September 4** — 1.3.1 Early Access opens for $9 tier testers\n• **September 14** — Public release for everyone\n\n# **The new policy** (see image below)\n\nSingleplayer users lose nothing and gain something: Volumetric Clouds are no longer paywalled on Legacy SP, and Enhanced SP is untouched. The paid side moves to FiveM, where CoreFX ends up running in a server context. And the $9 tier stops being a feature paywall entirely — it's early access to updates now, not a gate on content.\n\n# **Why I'm doing this**\n\nI'd rather explain than quietly change the numbers.\n\nI'm trying to leave Ukraine, or at minimum move away from the capital region to somewhere quieter. A [military warehouse explosion near me](https://discord.com/channels/963349840681639946/963349840681639950/1542971191566929991) recently killed almost 40 people. I don't feel safe where I live anymore, and relocating takes money I don't currently have.\n\nThis was the most honest way I could find to fund that: shift the paid part to FiveM, and make singleplayer more complete than it was before rather than less. I didn't want to solve my problem by taking something away from the people who have been using this mod for free.\n\nCoreFX remains what it has always been — a personal project, not a service. No roadmap, no requests, no promises about what gets worked on next. That doesn't change. Development continues either way.\n\nThank you to everyone who has supported this. It matters more than usual right now.\n\n— CoreFX",
